{"type":"message","id":"57515607","parentId":"fb0c2219","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:49:27.032Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass.\n\n**Cause:** `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")` only matches timestamps with no timezone, so the trailing `Z` in `\"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z\"` was left over and raised the error.\n\n**Fix:** `parse_date` now changes a trailing `Z` to `+00:00` and parses with `datetime.fromisoformat`. Python only accepts `Z` there from 3.11, so the swap makes it work on older versions too.\n\n**One behaviour change:** timestamps ending in `Z` or an offset now come back timezone-aware (UTC). Timestamps without one still come back naive, as before.\n\n- Comparing an aware datetime with a naive one, or subtracting one from the other, raises a `TypeError`. Any code that mixes the two from this feed will need to handle that.\n- `day_key` still returns the date exactly as written, with no timezone conversion."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":350,"cacheRead":26936,"cacheWrite":130,"totalTokens":27418,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":130}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277362728,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dFNr6ebhje3JJ96Mvh","duration":4303.366141000002,"ttft":4277.912677,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":27068,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
